From 87c6cda9410dd19a54ad5363353fbd8602e0bcaa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: boxwrench <westsunset@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 11:35:23 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] ROCm/gfx1201 compatibility + 1.3B causal-fast config

- attention: add _sdpa_attention, a semantically-equivalent PyTorch SDPA
  replacement for flash_attn_varlen_func (padding/window/causal masks,
  GQA expansion, q_scale/softmax_scale), and route flash_attention() and
  attention() through it when neither FlashAttention 2 nor 3 is importable.
  FlashAttention has no CUDA-free build; AMD needs this path.
  SDPA's is_causal aligns top-left while FA aligns bottom-right, so the
  fast path is only taken when Lq == Lk.
- attention: drop the q.device.type == 'cuda' assert (redundant on ROCm,
  where HIP tensors already report 'cuda', and it blocks CPU unit tests).
- configs: add i2v-1.3B, derived from the published 1.3b-causal-fast
  safetensors headers. Upstream ships no config for this variant.
- image2video/generate: allow an empty *_checkpoint to mean 'shards at the
  repository root', which is how the 1.3B release is laid out.
